coder › Fixed `slugify('Crème Brûlée')` → `'creme-brulee'` on branch `fix/slugify-accents`.

What changed:
- `src/slugify.ts`: added `.normalize('NFD')` + `.replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '')` before lowercasing, so accented Latin letters reduce to their base letter before the existing `[^a-z0-9]+` → `-` collapsing and dash-trimming logic (commits: `f4be6ac`, `d835b88`). The rest of the pipeline (runs of non-alphanumerics become one dash, leading/trailing dashes dropped, `''`/punctuation-only → `''`) was already correct and is unchanged.
- `src/slugify.test.ts`: added 5 tests — accented input, run collapsing (`'Hello,  World!'` → `'hello-world'`), dash trimming, empty string, punctuation-only.

Decision not in the request: chose NFD decomposition + stripping U+0300–U+036F combining marks rather than a manual accent map; non-decomposable letters (e.g. `ø`, `ß`, CJK) still fall through to the existing dash/empty rules.

